  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nUpper-level zonal flow will persist through the rest of the week \nwith near-normal temperatures and generally dry conditions expected. \nThere is a chance for light rain along the Continental Divide into \nportions of North-Central Montana but rainfall amounts are expected \nto be minimal.\n\nUpper-level ridging starts to build early next week which may allow \nfor a brief warm up to above normal temperatures before another \nupper-level trough arrives bringing temperatures back down to normal \nby the middle of the week.\n\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nShowers will try to form along the Continental Divide on Wednesday \nand Thursday but the expected moisture is going to be around a \ncouple hundredths at best with dry conditions expected to continue \nthrough at least the next 5 days.\n\nThe next chance for elevated fire weather conditions is currently \nMonday with highs in the upper 70s to low 80s, minimum RH values in \nthe 20s and wind gusts in the 20-30 mph range. Nothing looks \ncritical enough to warrant any elevated concerns at this time but it \nwill be something to watch with future updates. -thor",
